# Backend Development Rules

## Scope

Only modify code directly related to the requested feature.

Never modify unrelated business logic.

Never expand the scope.

---

## Existing Code First

Always search for existing implementations.

Reuse existing:

- services
- repositories
- DTOs
- validators
- utilities
- helpers

Never duplicate logic.

---

## File Management

Never create:

- Service
- Repository
- DTO
- Entity
- Utility
- Helper
- Config

without user approval.

---

## Architecture

Respect the existing architecture.

Never introduce a different architecture.

Never move business logic between layers.

Keep responsibilities clear.

---

## Code Quality

Write production-ready code.

Keep methods focused.

Keep classes focused.

Avoid unnecessary abstraction.

Avoid overengineering.

Prefer simple and maintainable solutions.

---

## Database

Never change:

- database schema
- entities
- migrations
- relationships

without explicit user approval.

Never modify SQL unless requested.

---

## API

Do not change API contracts unless requested.

Do not change request or response structures without approval.

Maintain backward compatibility whenever possible.